# ai-review global config — sourced as bash by ~/.local/bin/ai-review.
# Per-repo settings live in <repo>/.ai-review/config and override these.

# ----- Claude profile ------------------------------------------------
# Which Claude Code profile dir to use. ai-review always invokes `claude`;
# this just sets CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR for the invocation, so you can keep
# multiple profiles (personal/work, Anthropic/Bedrock, account A/B)
# separate per project.
AI_PROFILE_DIR="${AI_PROFILE_DIR:-$HOME/.claude}"

# Logical label for the profile — appears in logs and the run registry.
# Free-form. Use whatever helps you tell profiles apart at a glance:
# "personal" / "work" / "bedrock" / "default" / etc.
AI_CMD="${AI_CMD:-default}"

# Optional model override. Blank = let Claude pick its default. Set this
# only when you want a specific model id (commonly when AI_PROFILE_DIR
# points at an adapter that maps Claude → a different backend).
# AI_MODEL="claude-sonnet-4-6"

# ----- Pre-launch hook -----------------------------------------------
# Optional shell command run before the first reviewer fires. Useful when
# AI_CMD relies on a local adapter / proxy / tmux session.
#
# SECURITY: AI_PRELAUNCH is honored ONLY from this global config (or from
# the inline shell env). A per-repo .ai-review/config that tries to set
# AI_PRELAUNCH is ignored with a warning — otherwise a collaborator with
# merge access to one of your repos could plant arbitrary shell that
# fires every time you run ai-review there.
#
# Examples (illustrative — replace placeholders with your own values):
#   AI_PRELAUNCH='lsof -i :<PORT> -t >/dev/null || tmux new-session -d -s adapter "node ~/adapter/server.js"'
#   AI_PRELAUNCH='aws sso login --profile work'
# AI_PRELAUNCH=""

# ----- Per-call timeout ----------------------------------------------
# Default seconds-per-reviewer-call. Each reviewer can override by
# passing an explicit value to call_claude. Bump this if you're using
# a slow remote / a large model that thinks for a long time.
AI_TIMEOUT="${AI_TIMEOUT:-600}"

# ----- Review banner -------------------------------------------------
# Markdown prepended to the review body. Set to empty string to disable.
# AI_REVIEW_BANNER='> **Automated review** from the `ai-review` pipeline.
# > Findings are LLM-generated — apply judgment before acting on them.'

# ----- Identity for posting the review -------------------------------
# - "auto"    → use a GitHub App if ~/.config/ai-review/apps/<owner>__<repo>.conf
#               exists, otherwise fall back to your gh-cli login
# - "app"     → require a GitHub App (errors out if missing)
# - "gh-user" → always post under your gh-cli login
AI_REVIEW_IDENTITY="${AI_REVIEW_IDENTITY:-auto}"
